BOINC docker_wrapper: timestamps and durations in the task's stderr.

The wrapper's log in the task's stderr had no times, so it was hard to tell where a
task spent its time (image pull and build, container run, cleanup), e.g. when a 4 GB
image pull was interrupted after 10 minutes.
 - every message of the wrapper starts with the local time ("2026-11-01 13:47:31 ...",
   the format of BOINC's own "called boinc_finish" line)
 - DOCKER_CONN::command (lib/util.cpp) logs the time of each docker/podman command
   and "command finished after N s" (verbose mode, as the wrapper uses it)
 - the wrapper logs when the container has exited, with exit code and CPU time
Written for server_release/1.6/1.6.2 on top of 0002, 0004 and 0005.

